 180: ### 3.2 Beat and composition types
 181: 
 182: ```ts
 183: type Representation = {
 184:   paragraphId: Id; modality: "text" | "visual" | "camera" | "transition";
 185:   description: string;
 186: };
 187: type CameraPose = { x: number; y: number; zoom: number; rotate: number };
 188: type SafeCamera = { maxPanX: number; maxPanY: number; maxZoom: number; maxTilt: number };
 189: type Transform = {
 190:   x: number; y: number; z: number; scaleX: number; scaleY: number; rotate: number;
 191: };
 192: type Crop = { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number };
 193: type Responsive = { focalPoint: [number, number]; portraitCrop: Crop; landscapeCrop: Crop };
 194: type Beat = {
 195:   id: Id; order: number; seq: number;
 196:   type: "quote" | "dialogue" | "commentary" | "mixed" | "title" | "transition";
 197:   text: {
 198:     quote?: TextSelection;
 199:     dialogue?: (Dialogue & { speakerDisplayName: string })[];
 200:     commentary?: Commentary[];
 201:   };
 202:   compositionId: Id;
 203:   camera: {
 204:     from: CameraPose; to: CameraPose; durationMs: number;
 205:     easing: "linear" | "easeInOut" | "spring"; focusLayerId?: Id;
 206:     focusEntityId?: Id; rationale: string;
 207:   };
 208:   transitionIn: {
 209:     type: "cut" | "fade" | "slide" | "zoomThrough" | "parallaxShift";
 210:     durationMs: number;
 211:   };
 212:   inspectables: { entityId: Id; hotspot: Hotspot }[];
 213:   autoAdvanceMs?: number; representations: Representation[];
 214: };
 215: type DepthAsset = AssetRef & {
 216:   bitDepth: 8 | 16; sourceBitDepth: 8 | 16;
 217:   convention: "near-white"; provenance: "generated" | "derived";
 218: };
 219: type Layer = {
 220:   layerId: Id; role: "background" | "midground" | "foreground"; entityId?: Id;
 221:   image: AssetRef; mask?: AssetRef; depth?: DepthAsset; hiddenAreaImage?: AssetRef;
 222:   zOrder: number; depthRange: [number, number]; transform: Transform;
 223:   renderMode: "plane" | "depthMesh";
 224:   mesh?: { segmentsX: number; segmentsY: number; displacementScale: number };
 225: };
 226: type ReferencePin = { entityId: Id; stateId?: Id; version: number; s3Keys: string[]; checksum: string };
 227: type Composition = Lineage & {
 228:   schemaVersion: 1; compositionId: Id; revisionId: Id; reuseKey: string;
 229:   originEpisodeId: Id; usedIn: { episodeId: Id; momentId: Id; beatId: Id; revisionId: Id }[];
 230:   shotSnapshot: Shot; entityStatesUsed: EntityState[]; continuityRefs: string[];
 231:   referenceVersions: ReferencePin[]; visualProfileVersion: number;
 232:   master: AssetRef; depth?: DepthAsset; layers: Layer[];
 233:   safeCamera: SafeCamera; responsive: Responsive;
 234:   qa: {
 235:     textDetected: boolean; agreementScore: number | null;
 236:     identityScores: Record<Id, number>; issues: string[];
 237:     continuityStatus: "pending" | "approved" | "rejected";
 238:     approvedBy?: string; approvedAt?: IsoDate;
 239:   };
 240:   generation: {
 241:     provider: string; model: string; prompt: string; negativePrompt: string;
 242:     seed?: number; referenceKeys: string[]; costUsd: number;
 243:   };
 244:   status: "generated" | "approved" | "rejected" | "composed" | "published";
 245:   createdAt: IsoDate; updatedAt: IsoDate;
 246: };
 247: ```
 248: 
 249: Dialogue and commentary are text representations, not extra Representation.modality values. A coverage validator checks IDs and meaningful links; grounded AI review plus editorial preview confirms semantic fidelity. A camera pan alone cannot stand in for an unexpressed internal thought.
 250: Each Beat has exactly one compositionId. Draft IDs can name planned compositions pending assets; publication requires all references to resolve. Approximate 60-word quote screens split into ordered Beats, never truncate. Dialogue shows short exchanges; subtitles do not auto-advance unless explicitly timed by the plan, with reader-controlled pause/advance supported.
 251: Camera x/y are signed fractions of the composition width/height from its center; zoom=1 is the fitted viewport view and must be >=1; rotate/maxTilt are radians around the screen normal. Positive x is right, positive y is down. The name maxTilt is retained for the 2D camera rotation bound; do not silently reinterpret it as a free 3D orbit.
 252: Transform x/y follow the same center origin, z is normalized scene depth, scaleX/scaleY are positive multipliers, rotate radians. Hotspot/crop coordinates are normalized top-left x/y with w/h extents contained in [0,1]. Focal points use this same top-left frame.
 253: DepthRange uses [far,near] with values in [0,1]; larger zOrder/z/depth is closer. Overlapping depth ranges are allowed for real geometry; require valid monotonic ranges and consistent occlusion ordering rather than inventing disjoint-depth physics.
 254: depthMesh requires depth plus bounded integer subdivisions and finite displacementScale; planes may omit depth and mesh. Convert depth using explicit near-white convention; never treat depth or alpha data as color-managed photographs.
 255: A 16-bit depth asset is preferred when the provider genuinely supplies that precision. Converting 8-bit data to a 16-bit container must retain sourceBitDepth=8, never claim recovered detail. Full mesh support does not justify fabricated depth-quality scores.
 256: Master is the flattened composite/thumbnail derived from the approved layer assembly; it is not a competing scene source. Optional master depth cannot substitute for each depthMesh layer's aligned depth.
 257: All layers share an explicit composition canvas/perspective and keep transparent padding/placement consistent. Validate actual alpha, dimensions, masks/depth alignment and background overscan. Generate clean backgrounds so hidden areas exist; hiddenAreaImage is only needed when a further generated repair is required.
 258: safeCamera is computed from actual opaque/background coverage, crop/aspect, all layer movement, rotation and displacement limits. Metadata claims alone are not proof of hole-free motion. AI replans or regeneration resolves unsafe shots; owners never fix camera directions.
 259: Do not assume image conditioning guarantees identity equality; store actual review results and pending/null scores when no check exists.
