 304: 
 305: EpisodeBundle.entities is safe at episode start, not episode end. entityViews[beatId] is the resolved safe view at that Beat's seq; inspectables use that view, never raw canonical entities. Summaries/previews also must avoid leaking future revelations. Bundle data is downloadable for the episode: this is display spoiler safety, not DRM.
 306: Publish only allowlisted public fields. Do not export model prompts, jobs, emails, private facts, unpublished candidates or generation cost records.
 307: BookCatalog, not stale prev/next fields inside immutable bundles, determines currently available neighboring episodes. Use versioned catalog objects plus a small revalidated active pointer; long-lived immutable caching belongs to versioned assets/bundles only.
 308: External Reader sessions pin a version while reading. Stable IDs persist when meaning is unchanged; changed/split/deleted Beats get explicit progress anchors, falling back to source seq within the same sourceId. Cross-source progress mapping is explicit or unresolved, never a silently reused paragraph ID.
 309: Visual regeneration yields a new Composition/revision and updates draft usedIn references. Published bundles retain their exact composition snapshots/asset keys.
 310: Approval gates bind to content fingerprints, sourceId, visualProfile/reference versions and relevant plan revision. Async job completion must compare these pins before promotion; outdated work cannot regain approval.
