 312: ## 4. Persistence, immutability and module boundaries
 313: 
 314: | Path | Owner and purpose |
 315: |---|---|
 316: | books/{bookId} | Server-owned active source, structure/stats, visualProfile, pipeline and publication summaries. |
 317: | books/{bookId}/sources/{sourceId} | Extraction staging and correction history; never destroy approved source versions. |
 318: | books/{bookId}/textChunks/{sourceId}__{chunkId} | Version-keyed canonical projection; logical chunkId c0001, c0002, etc., normally 20 paragraphs. Query by activeSourceId. |
 319: | books/{bookId}/entities/{entityId} | Current source model proposal/approval. |
 320: | books/{bookId}/entities/{entityId}/visualVersions/{versionId} | Immutable approved reference metadata; S3 contains the assets. |
 321: | books/{bookId}/events/{eventId} | Source-grounded event model. |
 322: | books/{bookId}/derived/storyMap | Current source StoryMap. |
 323: | books/{bookId}/derived/ledger | Pointer/checkpoint summary; large per-window snapshots in Firebase Storage. |
 324: | books/{bookId}/episodes/{episodeId} | Current working Episode and active revision pointer; private editorial document. |
 325: | books/{bookId}/episodes/{episodeId}/moments/{momentId} | Current working Moment with readingBeats, source/revision pins. |
 326: | books/{bookId}/episodes/{episodeId}/revisions/{revisionId} | Revision manifest and immutable snapshot pointer; large episode snapshots in Storage/S3, not one oversized Firestore document. |
 327: | books/{bookId}/compositions/{compositionId} | Composition metadata and canonical usedIn reuse relationships. |
 328: | books/{bookId}/jobs/{jobId} | Individual durable job with bounded checkpoint metadata. |
 329: | books/{bookId}/published/{episodeId} | Sanitized active PublishedPointer. |
 330: | books/{bookId}/usage/{yyyymm} | Token/image spend totals derived idempotently from job/call records. |
 331: 
 332: Firebase Storage source: `books/{bookId}/sources/{sourceId}/original/{fileName}`.
 333: Firebase Storage canonical: `books/{bookId}/sources/{sourceId}/text/canonical.json`; never overwrite after approval.
 334: Ledger checkpoints: `books/{bookId}/sources/{sourceId}/ledger/{jobId}/{window}.json`.
 335: AWS assets: `books/{bookId}/assets/{assetVersionId}/{role}.{extension}`.
 336: AWS published: `books/{bookId}/published/{episodeId}/v{version}/bundle.json` and `manifest.json`.
 337: AWS catalogs: `books/{bookId}/catalog/v{version}.json`; Book.publishing.catalogKey is the trusted active discovery pointer.
 338: AWS drafts: `books/{bookId}/drafts/{episodeId}/{revisionId}/...`; do not infer drafts are private merely from this prefix. Local tests use a fake asset store; production delivery authorization must distinguish drafts from published assets before exposure.
 339: All generated reference/layer/depth/mask/variant/thumbnail assets go to S3, not Firebase Storage. Canonical source and ledger remain Firebase Storage. Firestore holds keys/hashes/review state only.
 340: Stage source-specific chunks first, validate their canonical hash and count, then atomically advance Book.activeSourceId/canonical. Physical chunk keys are source-versioned to avoid replacing chunks while the old active source is still selected.

