 346: ## 5. Visual planning, cameras and faithful reading
 347: 
 348: Planning selects semantic targets (character, object, location, reveal), framing, transitions, timing and normalized camera intent based on Book Model â†’ StoryMap â†’ Moment â†’ Beat. Layer IDs become concrete after generation; assembly resolves them and computes actual limits.
 349: The owner does not set camera direction, zoom, layer position, prompts or shot descriptions. Diagnostic depth/layer inspection is read-only in the primary workflow.
 350: References use canonical facts plus explicitly labelled fills; state/reveal-specific references must match both storyTime and seq. The image-generation request pins visualProfile and reference versions.
 351: Background generation includes the parts that become visible behind foreground assets. Foreground candidates need real alpha, not a drawn checkerboard. Generated depth must align with the exact image and preserve truthful bit-depth metadata.
 352: Regenerate at asset/layer/composition scope; a failed layer does not require discarding every approved sibling. Reference changes flag dependent drafts but never mutate published assets.
 353: Verification has two levels: deterministic schema/coverage/asset/camera checks and grounded/visual review. AI quality scores are evidence, not a mathematical guarantee of story fidelity or visual equality.
 354: Every story paragraph appears in a coverage report linking source â†’ Moment â†’ Beat â†’ Representation. Non-story material has explicit classification and remains available as source. The experience must not present itself as a summary/abridgment.
 355: Quote/dialogue text is exact; commentary has supported sentence-level citations and spoiler checks. Preserve negation, causality, attribution, internal thoughts and chronology; if camera/visual alone cannot carry them, use subtitles.
 356: Rendering uses an orthographic composition frame for WebGL planes/meshes. CSS fallback approximates planes/parallax and supported transitions; depth displacement degrades to flat layers with the same text, source order and controls.
 357: Respect reduced motion; default to user-driven reading without arbitrary timed advancement. Provide keyboard and touch navigation, readable subtitle safe areas, contrast and portrait/landscape wrapping. Sanitize any formatting; do not inject model-produced HTML through unchecked innerHTML.
 358: Preview scopes use the same coordinate/easing/crop/text/transition rules as exported data. No editor-only interpretation that makes an invalid bundle look valid.
 359: 
 360: ## 6. Pipeline and approval gates
 361: 
 362: | Stage | Automatic work | Owner-facing action |
 363: |---|---|---|
 364: | Source | Extract/layout/OCR, paragraph order/classification, chapter proposal and validation | Review source; approve extraction. Failed steps offer retry/AI repair, not required forms. |
 365: | Understand/consolidate | Chapter-bounded rolling ledger, facts/events/states/reveals, alias candidates and chronology | Review/approve Book Model; disputed proposals return to AI regeneration. |
 366: | Map/plan | StoryMap, Episode ranges, episode storyPlan and scene Moments | Review/approve StoryMap and episode plans. |
 367: | Build Beats | Grounded text, paragraph representations, semantic cameras/transitions and composition recipes | Preview planned Beats; review/approve content. |
 368: | Visual references | AI drafts visualProfile/specs/reference prompts and target lists | Generate one/select multiple references; approve candidates/style. |
 369: | Scene visuals | Requests use only approved pinned references | Generate one/select multiple visual targets; regenerate failures; approve continuity. |
 370: | Compose | Assemble planes/depthMesh, responsive crops, camera limits and validation automatically | Preview Beat/Moment/Episode; approve assembled result. |
 371: | Publish | Validate/compile/upload immutable version and prepare atomic promotion | Explicit approve and publish; readers can access this Episode independently. |
 372: | Replacement | AI updates only affected draft assets/assembly and approval fingerprints | Regenerate â†’ compare â†’ approve replacement; previous version stays live. |
 373: 
 374: Planning jobs continue after prerequisites are approved, not after extra manual data entry. No visual-image API calls run merely because a user opens a page.
 375: Preserve cost limits and explicit over-budget confirmation; cap automatic plan-repair attempts and show actionable failures. Single and batch visuals share the same prompt/validation/approval path.
 376: Current LLM/image configuration stays; model choices are configuration, not required per-shot inputs. All provider calls are validated and checkpointed; only current approved reference versions may be used.
 377: Callbacks carry jobId/idempotencyKey and expected revision; retry is not a new billable regeneration. Explicit regeneration is a new attempt with a distinct idempotency key.
 378: 
 379: ## 7. Studio surfaces and direct preview
 380: 
 381: Library shows each book's stage, active job and published episodes. Book overview exposes one next action plus exact clickable blockers.
 382: Book Model: Entity table/type filters, facts versus fills, states/reveals/relationships, reference status, Event list/chronology and provenance. AI merge/split proposals are approve/reject actions; no required manual field editing.
 383: StoryMap: acts/arcs, chronology and paragraph timeline with proposed Episode boundaries. Underlying neighbor-boundary validation is retained, but AI owns changes; owner approves or requests a revised plan.
 384: Episode board: Moment scene ranges, stage status, coverage and production readiness. Focused Moment/Beat review replaces large nested editing cards.
 385: Visual review: approved versioned references beside generated candidates, multi-select generation, targeted regeneration and affected-dependency status.
 386: 2.5D review: read-only layer/depth inspector and parallax scrub; AI cameras displayed with their source-backed purpose. Do not ship a required Set camera step.
 387: Preview panel: Beat/Moment/Episode scope, play/pause/replay/scrub/next/previous, subtitle and motion controls, plus working/published/compare modes.
 388: Scope selection immediately loads a renderable preview; playback obeys user/reduced-motion preferences and does not auto-start paid work.
 389: Draft preview can show explicit missing-layer/asset placeholders; those placeholders can never count as approved/publishable assets.
 390: Loading, empty, failed, partial, outdated, ready-for-review and approved states are distinct. Every blocker has a named target and useful action: approve reference, generate selected, regenerate layer, retry AI planning, preview or compare.
 391: Approval controls show what stage they unlock. Reopen/reject/regenerate invalidates relevant draft approvals explicitly; it never silently unpublishes the current episode.
 392: Publication checklist is entirely derived from validators, reference approvals and content/preview fingerprints; no manual checkbox may bypass a failing invariant.
 393: Acceptance: from upload to publication an owner can finish using approval, visual selection/generation and preview only. Never force the owner to type JSON, fields, camera values, prompts or repair text.
