 661: ## Rollback and abort
 662: 
 663: - Never git commit/push/deploy. Preserve the existing dirty worktree and untracked new.md.
 664: - Before each phase, inventory tracked changes and untracked source files and record the baseline in the progress log without dumping secrets.
 665: - Save a binary-safe tracked patch at `.patches/<phase>-studio.patch` using `git diff --binary --output=<path>`. Also save newly created non-secret source/test files as individual no-index binary patches or explicit copies under that phase's snapshot directory; plain git diff omits untracked files. Do not stage files just to make snapshots.
 666: - A cumulative patch against HEAD is evidence, not a clean per-phase reversal. Record each phase's changed-file list and preserve its starting snapshot so selective recovery can distinguish owner changes and earlier phases.
 667: - No git reset --hard, git checkout -- ., broad recursive deletion or whole-worktree restore. Rollback is an owner-reviewed selective restore against the relevant before/after snapshot.
 668: - If a dependency did not land, implement only independent in-scope work, label any placeholder honestly, and finish qa-pending with the missing proof named. Never fake successful generation, approval or publication.
 669: - If the plan itself is contradictory, log the exact contradiction in status.md Deferred and stop that phase; executing sessions cannot rewrite plan.md/CONTEXT.md to hide it.
 670: - Failed/skipped gates cannot yield done. Use qa-pending only for complete code with named verification gaps; blocked means the required work did not land.
 671: - The runner performs a final read-only AUDIT and writes QA.md; it does not make unresolved work production-ready.

