 379: ## 7. Studio surfaces and direct preview
 380: 
 381: Library shows each book's stage, active job and published episodes. Book overview exposes one next action plus exact clickable blockers.
 382: Book Model: Entity table/type filters, facts versus fills, states/reveals/relationships, reference status, Event list/chronology and provenance. AI merge/split proposals are approve/reject actions; no required manual field editing.
 383: StoryMap: acts/arcs, chronology and paragraph timeline with proposed Episode boundaries. Underlying neighbor-boundary validation is retained, but AI owns changes; owner approves or requests a revised plan.
 384: Episode board: Moment scene ranges, stage status, coverage and production readiness. Focused Moment/Beat review replaces large nested editing cards.
 385: Visual review: approved versioned references beside generated candidates, multi-select generation, targeted regeneration and affected-dependency status.
 386: 2.5D review: read-only layer/depth inspector and parallax scrub; AI cameras displayed with their source-backed purpose. Do not ship a required Set camera step.
 387: Preview panel: Beat/Moment/Episode scope, play/pause/replay/scrub/next/previous, subtitle and motion controls, plus working/published/compare modes.
 388: Scope selection immediately loads a renderable preview; playback obeys user/reduced-motion preferences and does not auto-start paid work.
 389: Draft preview can show explicit missing-layer/asset placeholders; those placeholders can never count as approved/publishable assets.
 390: Loading, empty, failed, partial, outdated, ready-for-review and approved states are distinct. Every blocker has a named target and useful action: approve reference, generate selected, regenerate layer, retry AI planning, preview or compare.
 391: Approval controls show what stage they unlock. Reopen/reject/regenerate invalidates relevant draft approvals explicitly; it never silently unpublishes the current episode.
 392: Publication checklist is entirely derived from validators, reference approvals and content/preview fingerprints; no manual checkbox may bypass a failing invariant.
 393: Acceptance: from upload to publication an owner can finish using approval, visual selection/generation and preview only. Never force the owner to type JSON, fields, camera values, prompts or repair text.
