   1: # Project Context â€” Visual Book Platform Studio
   2: 
   3: Confirmed with the owner on 2026-09-18; the current feature plan is `docs/features/25d-schema-foundation/plan.md`.
   4: This document distinguishes inspected legacy implementation from the confirmed target. Executing sessions use these names verbatim and do not add or rewrite ADRs; proposed changes go to feature status.md Deferred.
   5: 
   6: ## Product and boundaries
   7: 
   8: Studio is the internal editorial production application in `C:/Users/800sa/studio`. It turns a complete source book into approved, ordered 2.5D assets and episode bundles.
   9: The external Reader is a separate web application and is not built in this repository.
  10: Studio Preview renders the Reader data contract for editorial inspection of Beats, Moments and Episodes. It is not a consumer library/account/payment product.
  11: The Pipeline Worker executes long-running, checkpointed jobs independently of Next.js.
  12: After uploading a source, the owner reviews/approves and selects visuals for single/batch generation or regeneration. AI supplies the plans, text, prompts, camera motion, transitions and assembly.
  13: 
  14: ## Vocabulary
  15: 
  16: | Name | Exact meaning |
  17: |---|---|
  18: | Book | Root metadata, active source, book-wide style, pipeline and publication identity. |
  19: | SourceRevision | One extraction/correction staging revision; approved canonical text is immutable within that sourceId. |
  20: | Paragraph | Canonical source unit with id, global seq, chapterId, text/hash, kind and isStory. |
  21: | seq | Zero-based position in canonical book order and the coordinate for reveal safety; never chronology. |
  22: | storyTime | In-story chronology ordinal used to resolve entity state; flashbacks do not reorder playback. |
  23: | canonical.json | Complete source-specific canonical paragraph text in Firebase Storage. |
  24: | Entity | Character, location, object or group with facts, fills, states, reveals, relationships and visual references. |
  25: | Fact | A sourced claim, with paragraph evidence and earliest known seq. |
  26: | Fill | An explicitly invented visual choice where source text is silent; never presented as a sourced fact. |
  27: | Event | Source-grounded occurrence with seq range, storyTime and entity participants. |
  28: | ledger | Rolling registry built by the understanding pass; each window has a resumable checkpoint. |
  29: | StoryMap | Acts, arcs, chronology and proposed contiguous Episode ranges. |
  30: | Episode | Ordered publication unit containing Moments and their Beats; independently publishable. |
  31: | Moment | Scene unit with continuous time, stable cast/location and a contiguous source range. |
  32: | Beat | Reading/playback step: structured subtitle text, exactly one composition, AI camera motion, transition and inspectables. |
  33: | Representation | Explicit description linking a paragraph to text, visual, camera or transition expression in a Beat. Dialogue/commentary are text forms. |
  34: | Composition | Reusable source/reference-pinned scene with master, layers, optional depth, safe camera bounds, responsive framing and continuity approval. |
  35: | Layer | Independently rendered background/midground/foreground asset using plane or depthMesh mode. |
  36: | depthMesh | A runtime subdivided layer mesh displaced by its aligned depth texture; not a separately authored geometry file. |
  37: | visualProfile | Versioned book-wide art direction and constraints. |
  38: | VisualReferenceVersion | Immutable approved entity/state/location reference assets and metadata. |
  39: | ReferencePin | Exact approved reference version/keys/hash used for generation. |
  40: | safeCamera | Deterministically computed motion limits based on actual scene coverage and displacement. |
  41: | Job | One durable Firestore work item with lease, retries, progress, checkpoints and costs. |
  42: | Working revision | Mutable editorial replacement candidate, separate from the active published Episode version. |
  43: | EpisodeBundle | Immutable, schema-versioned resolved playback data and asset references for one Episode. |
  44: | EpisodeManifest | Asset/checksum/size list and progress-anchor metadata for one published version. |
  45: | PublishedPointer | Sanitized active version pointer switched only after complete upload and approval. |
  46: | BookCatalog | Versioned ordered list of independently published Episodes; authority for next-episode discovery. |
  47: | WorkflowAction | A next-step button or a blocker-resolution action with an explicit target and validation state. |
  48: 
  49: Identifiers follow new.md: p000000 onwards for canonical paragraphs; ch_/loc_/obj_/grp_ for entities; ep_01, ep_01_m01, ep_01_m01_b01 initially; cmp_ content/version hash for compositions; L0 background to nearer layers.
  50: Published IDs stay stable when meaning stays stable. Display order is separate. Paragraph IDs only identify text together with sourceId/canonicalHash.
  51: 
  52: ## Inspected legacy vocabulary
  53: 
  54: - Book Bible/BibleEntry: generic kind/name/aliases/fields entries under a SourceRevision. Target Entity/Event/StoryMap is a semantic replacement, not a mechanical rename.
  55: - EpisodePlan: source-scoped paragraph-ID start/end ranges with intentional-overlap/exclusion support. Target Episode uses strict canonical story coverage.
  56: - StoryMomentPlan: old many-to-many paragraph mappings, one primary text and one active image plus posting state. Target Moment is a scene container; Beat is the playback unit.
  57: - StyleCanon: existing book-wide visual rules; target visualProfile preserves the purpose with version pins.
  58: - jobs/allJobs: current one-document job map; target one document per Job.
  59: - Canonical Story Moments/live=true: legacy Firestore publication projection; target immutable AWS EpisodeBundle plus active published pointers.
  60: 
  61: ## Modules and evidence
  62: 
  63: - `src/app`: thin Next pages/routes; `src/proxy.ts` is an optimistic access check.
  64: - `src/features/<domain>/store.ts`: trusted server Firestore transactions, enqueueing and approvals.
  65: - `src/features/<domain>/types.ts`: current domain types/pure invariants; canonical schemas move to `src/features/book-experience/schemas/`.
  66: - `src/features/<domain>/components`: editorial UI; new feature domains own their hooks/functions/components.
  67: - `src/services/firebase`: admin/client boundary and live browser reads.
  68: - `worker/index.mts`: current poll/claim/dispatch/recovery entry; focused worker domain folders own new behavior.
  69: - `tests/smoke`: custom Node fixture tests; source-string UI/rules checks are not behavioral proof.
  70: - `tests/book-experience`: planned schema/preview/local integration tests; P2 creates browser prior art.

