+## Owner actions
+
+### NOW-BLOCKING
+
+1. Replace the synthetic WebGL/CSS renderers with canonical image/depth asset rendering and apply responsive crops, transforms, safe-camera output, and aspect ratios in both paths.
+2. Materialize immutable `canonical.json` and paragraph chunks in the production source-approval path; prove correction creates a new source/hash and invalidates downstream drafts without mutating published history.
+3. Wire the canonical durable job engine and P5–P9 review surfaces into the active worker/app. Remove the owner journey's dependency on manual prompt/camera/layer/text/data entry.
+4. Decode and validate generated asset bytes. Derive checksums, alpha, dimensions, depth precision/range, alignment, overscan, and text-detection results from actual files; require a real continuity decision.
+5. Enforce strict schemas and recomputed content fingerprints/source/hash/revision pins at every approval boundary. Make retry/double-click advancement idempotent.
+6. Integrate semantic Representation coverage and per-Beat spoiler views into the actual compiler/approval path.
+7. Implement P10 publication before treating the workflow as complete: independent Episode publication, immutable assets/bundles, atomic CAS promotion, historical retention, session pins, progress anchors, rollback, and withdrawal.
+8. Restore a passing real-browser preview run. Existing executable command:
+
+   ```text
+   npx.cmd playwright test tests/book-experience/preview.spec.ts --reporter=line
+   ```
+
+### BEFORE-DEPLOY
+
+1. Implement P11 sanitized public-read rules, indexes, and emulator tests. Demonstrate editor-only source/model/job data and read-only public artifacts. Do not treat `smoke:posting` as emulator evidence.
+2. Re-run the production-negative bypass checks and the development browser-readiness check against the intended local/emulator environment without interactive login. Do not mint or disclose a live token in an audit.
+3. Perform owner visual review with real validated assets on representative mobile devices: portrait/landscape crops, transparent edges, parallax/depth continuity, reduced motion, subtitle readability, WebGL failure, and CSS fallback.
+4. Add the planned publication gates when their implementation exists. `smoke:bundles` and `smoke:publishing` are not currently executable scripts and must not be reported as run.
+5. Re-run the existing safe matrix:
